# Product feeds are fetched byte-for-byte by Google and Pinterest, and the
# publisher verifies the served copy against a sha256 in feeds/manifest.json.
# Git EOL conversion breaks that: a Windows checkout gets CRLF while GitHub
# serves the LF bytes as committed, so the hashes disagree by ~200KB of line
# endings and every freshness check fails with "STALE SERVE" on a healthy feed.
#
# -text disables all EOL translation, so the working tree, the commit and the
# served file are the same bytes on every machine.
feeds/* -text
